119	   center sweeps a much larger diamond-shaped envelope), then back into
120	   alignment near 0/90/180/270deg. That's what read as "a giant blob that
121	   then disappears": it never disappeared, it was cycling through a much
122	   bigger silhouette than the box. The fix is to keep the ring's shape
123	   perfectly static and instead animate the *angle fed into the conic
124	   gradient* via a registered custom property (@property is required for
125	   the browser to animate it smoothly rather than snapping) — the ring
126	   never moves, only the color chases around inside it. */
