import { DatabaseSync } from "node:sqlite";

const db = new DatabaseSync("board.sqlite");

// Written from a file rather than an inline shell script: the previous attempt
// passed this text through bash, which treated the backticked code spans as
// command substitution and silently deleted them mid-sentence.
const body = `AUDIT LOG built and complete; RBAC and 2FA are NOT.

lib/admin-audit.ts + /admin/audit. Closed action vocabulary modelled on lib/events.ts, and all 16 admin surfaces now record — nine reads of customer data, seven writes. The vocabulary holds an emittedBy field per action, so /admin/audit renders its own outstanding-work list from data rather than from a comment nobody opens.

Two real bugs found in the process, both the same class:

1. PROTOTYPE-CHAIN HOLE. isAdminAction was written as:
       typeof v === "string" && v in ADMIN_ACTION_INFO
   The "in" operator walks the prototype chain, so ?action=toString passed a guard whose entire job is to say "this is one of ours". The page would then read a Function off Function.prototype and hand it to React. Fixed with Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call, and verified over HTTP: ?action=toString now renders unfiltered instead of filtering to zero.

2. A 500 ON LARGE PAGE NUMBERS. (page - 1) * 50 went straight to Prisma as skip. The author probed the real boundary rather than guessing — 5e18 is fine, 5e21 throws — then proved the fix by temporarily REMOVING the clamp and confirming the 500 came back. They also corrected their own comment mid-run after the test contradicted their first guess about an int32 limit.

THE SAME PROTOTYPE-CHAIN PATTERN WAS FOUND INDEPENDENTLY A SECOND TIME, in app/admin/sites: ?view=toString and ?sort=constructor produced three reachable 500s. One instance there was genuinely dangerous — reason=constructor was truthy, and would have been written into the audit log as the stated justification for a takedown. Two independent occurrences makes this worth grepping for wherever "in" is used as a membership guard.

Still missing from this card: RBAC (there is one ADMIN role with no granularity) and 2FA.

VOLUMETRIC WARNING before this ships: site.viewed records every render, and a short browsing session generated 144 audit rows. Worth deciding whether page views need sampling, or whether only writes and detail views should record.

STATUS: built and verified locally. NOT deployed — schema must be pushed to staging/prod first.`;

const row = db
  .prepare(
    "SELECT cm.id FROM comments cm JOIN cards c ON c.id = cm.cardId WHERE c.title LIKE '%Admin RBAC%' ORDER BY cm.createdAt DESC LIMIT 1",
  )
  .get();

db.prepare("UPDATE comments SET body = ? WHERE id = ?").run(body, row.id);

const check = db.prepare("SELECT body FROM comments WHERE id = ?").get(row.id);
console.log("rewritten:", row.id);
console.log("contains the code span:", check.body.includes("v in ADMIN_ACTION_INFO"));
console.log("contains hasOwnProperty:", check.body.includes("hasOwnProperty"));
console.log("length:", check.body.length);

